/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-open-files-in-linguist.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-tos.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-reference.html

    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-cpp
    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-qml

    \title Open TS files in \QL

    Design applications so that they can be adapted to various languages and
    regions without engineering changes. Mark UI text as translatable to create
    Qt translation source (TS) files that contain the strings, and start \l {\QL}
    to translate them.

    To open TS files in \QL:

    \list 1
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Explorer}, and select a \e {.ts} file.
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
            \uicontrol {Qt: Open current file in Linguist}.
        \li Use \QL to translate UI text.
    \endlist
*/
